Primary Key: Unique identifier for a record.
Foreign Key: Refers to primary key in another table (enforces relationships).
Candidate Key: All possible unique keys.
Composite Key: Primary key made from multiple attributes.
Super Key: Any set of attributes that uniquely identifies a record.

Example SQL:-
CREATE TABLE Student (
    RollNo INT PRIMARY KEY,
    Name VARCHAR(50),
    Class VARCHAR(10)
);

CREATE TABLE Marks (
    RollNo INT,
    Subject VARCHAR(50),
    Score INT,
    FOREIGN KEY (RollNo) REFERENCES Student(RollNo)
);

